# Git: work on `main`

- Check out and stay on **`main`** unless the user explicitly names another branch.
- Before starting work, run `git checkout main` and `git pull origin main` when the network is available.
- Do not create feature branches or open PRs unless the user asks.
- Commit directly on `main` when the user asks to commit (follow the repo commit message style).
- Avoid merging `main` into long-lived branches; bring changes onto `main` instead.
- Do not commit `.next/` build or cache output; limit commits to source and config.
